NoahMP 5.0 SNIP DA interface checks
=================================

Scope
-----
The SNIP callbacks are ported from NoahMP 4.0.1 at LISF master commit
95ae9791ab8f5774ea77957b9f125d0899177c1c. Model-independent SNIP behavior,
including QC and the snow-source diagnostic collection, is retained.
noahmp50_snip_update calls the existing noahmp50_usafsi_update, which uses
per-tile NoahMP 5.0 parameters and NoahMP50_snowphys_updateMod. This retains
the existing 5.0 snow DA physics, including its 5000 mm SWE limit, rather
than copying the 4.0.1 physics/parameter-table imports and 2000 mm limit.
The existing 4.0.1, USAFSI and SNODEP sources are unchanged.

Configuration
-------------
Use a configured NoahMP 5.0 EnKF run and select:

  Land surface model:                  "Noah-MP.5.0"
  Data assimilation algorithm:         "EnKF"
  Data assimilation set:               "SNIP"
  SNIP data directory:                 ./FORCING/SNIP
  SNIP netcdf filename prefix:         SNIP

These entries are a configuration fragment, not a complete runnable case.
The SNIP reader expects the existing prefix_yyyymmddhh.nc naming scheme.
Use the usual observation-domain, observation-error, ensemble and state
perturbation settings for the target experiment; this port does not tune
them. State attributes must contain SWE (mm) and Snowdepth (m), as in
lis/configs/557WW-7.6-FOC/7.6.1/NRT/attribs/noahmp_snow_attribs.txt.
SNIP observations and the snow-depth observation operator are in meters.
The SNIP reader, file format and unit handling are unchanged.

At build time enable NoahMP.5.0, EnKF and DA OBS SNIP. Rerun the LIS
configuration/build-path generation after updating default.cfg. Both
da_snip and da_usafsi are included in the NoahMP 5.0 DA build paths;
the USAFSI observation reader does not need to be enabled. Direct insertion
is not added by this port, matching the existing NoahMP 4.0.1 SNIP wiring.

Standalone checks
-----------------
From the repository root, with GNU Fortran and Python 3 available:

  git submodule update --init lis/surfacemodels/land/noahmp.5.0/phys/noahmp
  FC=gfortran python3 lis/testcases/dataassim/noahmp50_snip/run_checks.py

The script uses a temporary build directory and does not modify the source
tree. It exercises the real plugins.py build-path generator and plugin
preprocessor guards with SNIP enabled/disabled, NoahMP 4.0.1 selected, and
DA disabled. It compiles all 12 new Fortran files against the actual
NoahMP50_module, NoahMP50_lsmMod type declarations, Machine and
LisNoahmpParamType from the pinned NoahMP submodule. Only framework
initialization is omitted from the copied lsmMod; ESMF and LIS services
are minimal test doubles in stubs.F90.

Runtime checks cover snow-state extraction, the observation operator,
unchanged observation units, increment mapping, state update/QC, setting
model state, snow-source collection, snow creation and complete removal.
Snow/soil outputs from the SNIP update are compared with the existing
5.0 USAFSI update for zero, positive and negative increments. Bounds and
invalid/zero/overflow floating-point traps are enabled.

These checks establish interface compatibility and reuse of existing
behavior. They do not independently validate the inherited QC or snow
physics, exercise real ESMF/MPI, read an actual SNIP NetCDF file, or replace
a full LIS build and short run with real forcing, restart and SNIP inputs.
In particular, partial snow-removal physics is checked for equivalence
with the existing 5.0 updater, not for exact agreement with a target SWE
or snow depth. The inherited updater may adjust depth through compaction.
